--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.spaceship]/4: the usual arithmetic conversions are applied to
arithmetic operands of <=>.  The lowering to the comparison-category
constants compared the operands as given, so `(a == b) <=> true' -- a
comparison result (internal bool) against a C++ bool, the closing
`return (__first2 == __last2) <=> true;' of libstdc++ 16's
lexicographical_compare_three_way -- evaluated wrongly.
